   "front": "Khel Yatra Physical Education and Well-being Textbook for Grade 6 Prelims.indd 1 19-Jul-24 5:22:58 PM Reprint 2026-27",
   "chapters": [
    {
     "file": "feky101",
     "pages": 13,
     "head": "UNIT 1 In this unit, we will discover how regular physical activity can make us feel good and help us get along with others. Here’s what we will do: 1. Games and Fun Activities: We will play lots of fun games and have interesting discussions. 2. Looking after each other: We will learn to stay together, grow together and be happy for each other. We will also learn and explore how doing all that can make us happier, physically & mentally stronger and more successful. 3. Safety First: We will find out ways to: • stay safe while playing • avoid injuries • create a healthy environment for everyone. There are some traditional games which are best to inculcate different values and cultural understanding. Also, they help in making a player fit and alert. Let’s explore! Importance of Physical Education and Well-being Physical Education Unit 1.indd 1 20-Jul-24 2:54:24 PM Reprint 2026-27"
    },
    {
     "file": "feky102",
     "pages": 27,
     "head": "UNIT 2 Motor Fitness In this unit, we will learn about the importance of fitness. We will also understand that being fit can help us to be healthy and strong. Here are a few things we can do to be fit: 1. Endurance: We will do fun activities that will help us to play longer without getting tired. 2. Building strength: We will get stronger with regular exercise. It will build our muscles and bones. 3. Becoming flexible: When we stretch and move in guided ways, our bodies will become flexible. 4. Learning balance: When we practice being steady while playing and exercising, we also learn to balance our body. Let’s get moving and explore fitness with fun! Physical Education Unit 2.indd 14 20-Jul-24 2:56:53 PM Reprint 2026-27"
    },
    {
     "file": "feky103",
     "pages": 35,
     "head": "UNIT 3 Fundamental Skills of Kho-Kho In this unit, we will learn about an exciting Indian sport called Kho-Kho. This game is interesting and helps us to work together as a team. Kho-Kho is a sport where two teams compete. One team tries to tag members of the opponent team while they avoid being tagged. The game involves quick movement, agility, speed, leg strength and teamwork, with players taking turns to defend and chase. Here’s what we will do: 1. Learn and Play: We will have fun sessions where we will learn how to play Kho-Kho through interactive games and group exercises. 2. Develop Skills: We will do exciting lead up activities to develop kho-kho skills. 3. Work as a Team: We will focus on working together and supporting each other during the game. Let’s get ready to play, learn and enjoy the game of Kho-Kho! Physical Education Unit 3.indd 41 19-Jul-24 3:19:28 PM Reprint 2026-27"
    },
    {
     "file": "feky104",
     "pages": 33,
     "head": "UNIT 4 Fundamental Skills of Handball In this unit, we will learn about the game of handball. This is a fast-paced invasive team sport played with a ball. Players pass, dribble and shoot the ball to score points. Defence involves intercepting passes and blocking the shots. Here’s what we will do: 1. Learn and Play: We will learn how to play Handball through interactive games and exercises. 2. Better Coordination, Strength and Endurance: Handball will help us in improving our coordination, strength, and endurance. 3. Team Spirit: We will focus on working together , involving everyone, and supporting each other during the game. Let us get ready to play handball, work as a team and have fun! Physical Education Unit 4.indd 76 19-Jul-24 3:24:38 PM Reprint 2026-27"
    },
    {
     "file": "feky105",
     "pages": 102,
     "head": "UNIT 5 Welcome to the world of Yoga for holistic health and well-being. In this unit, let us explore the ancient art and science of Yoga – a practice that originated in India and endured for thousands of years. Passed down through generations in India, it is now enjoyed by people all around the world. Yoga Physical Education Unit 5.indd 109 19-Jul-24 3:33:51 PM Reprint 2026-27"
    }
